==Russian==

===Etymology===
Inherited from {{inh|ru|orv|черенъ}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*černъ}}. Cognate with {{cog|uk|че́рен||[[shank]], [[plowshare]]}}, also {{m|uk|чере́н}}; Russian Church Slavonic {{m|cu|чрѣнъ||[[handle]]}}; {{cog|bg|црен}}; {{cog|sh|цре̏н}}; {{cog/sl-tonal|črẹ̑n}}; {{cog|cs|střen||[[handle]]}}, also {{m|cs|střena}}, {{m|cs|třeň}}; {{cog|sk|črienka||[[knife]] [[handle]]}}; {{cog|pl|trzon||[[handle]], [[hilt]]}}, also {{m|pl|trzonek}}; {{cog|hsb|črjonk}}; {{cog|dsb|cŕonk}}. Per Vasmer, probably related to {{cog|ru|ко́рень||[[root]]}} as well as {{cog|lt|kẽras||[[bush]], [[root]], [[stump]]}}, {{cog|prg|kirno||[[bush]]}}, {{cog|grc|κράνος||[[cornelian cherry]]}}, {{cog|la|cornus||[[cornelian cherry]]}}.

